                                "sense_id": "43131034-92ce-32a0-89d6-79cbb6abde36",
                                "text": "Zilpha, being just Hiram's age, as was woman's right, blossomed first, and became a demure, marriageable little Mormoness in long dresses (or, as a perverse Gentile friend used to call Mormon little girls, a \"Mormoniculess,\" Mormon little boys being similarly \"Mormonicles\"),\" while Hiram was blushing at the shortness of a roundabout, which he felt still more ashamed to exchange for that uneasily self-conscious garment, a coat with tails."
